WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.469
-My next guest is a very
talented actor and comedian.

00:00:03.469 --> 00:00:05.371
He stars in the movie
"The Right One,"

00:00:05.371 --> 00:00:08.174
which is available now
on digital and on demand.

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:10.810
Here is Nick Thune!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:14.647
♪ -Better make room
for my man Nick Thune ♪

00:00:14.647 --> 00:00:16.582
♪ Serves jokes with a tune ♪

00:00:16.582 --> 00:00:19.118
♪ That's what you get
with Nick Thune ♪

00:00:19.118 --> 00:00:23.523
♪ Better make room
for my man Nick Thune ♪

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:25.458
♪ Jokes with a tune ♪

00:00:25.458 --> 00:00:28.995
♪ Nick Thune ♪

00:00:28.995 --> 00:00:32.999
-Nick, thank you for coming
in the studio to see us.

00:00:32.999 --> 00:00:34.600
It means a lot to us.
Welcome back.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:37.303
-Well, thanks, Jimmy.
I feel great here.

00:00:37.303 --> 00:00:39.873
-The last time you were on
the show, you were nice enough.

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:42.175
We were doing the show
from my home.

00:00:42.175 --> 00:00:44.710
And you were nice enough
to come on the show then.

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:49.048
And you had a very funny video
about homeschooling your son.

00:00:49.048 --> 00:00:50.416
How's everything
going with your son?

00:00:50.416 --> 00:00:53.385
Is it still difficult?
-You know, I have not seen him.

00:00:53.385 --> 00:00:55.354
He's been in juvie
for about six months.

00:00:55.354 --> 00:00:57.056
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, my God.

00:00:57.056 --> 00:00:58.924
Oh, my God. Oh, it's terrible.

00:00:58.924 --> 00:01:00.760
I'm sorry. What happened?

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:02.395
-People don't realize
how easy it is

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:05.230
to frame your kid for a crime.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.230 --> 00:01:07.099
-Wow. I did not know.

00:01:07.099 --> 00:01:09.269
-I just thought this is
a better school system for him.

00:01:09.269 --> 00:01:10.503
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.503 --> 00:01:11.838
-Good for you.
-Yeah.

00:01:11.838 --> 00:01:13.773
It's like going to a fun
summer camp all year.

00:01:13.773 --> 00:01:14.874
Yeah. That's the thing
I like about you.

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:16.142
You're not selfish, you know?

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:18.077
-No, no, no, no. Never.

00:01:18.077 --> 00:01:19.512
-I want to talk about --

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:21.580
I want to talk about
"The Right One," your movie.

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:23.816
I love seeing you act.

00:01:23.816 --> 00:01:26.753
I've said this before
because I was watching "Venom,"

00:01:26.753 --> 00:01:27.954
I want to say, the Marvel movie.

00:01:27.954 --> 00:01:29.622
-Yeah.
-You're in the Marvel Universe.

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:31.691
I saw you in "Venom,"
and I go --

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:34.127
Dude, that was fantastic.
What did that feel like?

00:01:34.127 --> 00:01:36.596
-Oh, my God, it was so good.
I had a role.

00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:38.531
The name was like Kevin,
you know?

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:39.698
-Wow.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.698 --> 00:01:41.501
Please sit down, everybody.
Please sit down.

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:42.668
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.668 --> 00:01:44.036
Everyone remembers Kevin.
-I played --

00:01:44.036 --> 00:01:46.339
Well, I was playing Kevin,
and then as a joke,

00:01:46.339 --> 00:01:47.907
because the scene was in a bar

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:50.843
and I was, like, joking with
Tom, my buddy Tom Hardy.

00:01:50.843 --> 00:01:53.680
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, my God.

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:55.048
-And I said that'd be funny

00:01:55.048 --> 00:01:59.152
if my name was Beardo at the Bar
instead of Kevin.

00:01:59.152 --> 00:02:01.186
-Yeah.
-And the director heard that.

00:02:01.186 --> 00:02:04.323
So somehow in the credits
it does say Beardo at the Bar

00:02:04.323 --> 00:02:07.293
now instead of Kevin,
if you like, look me up on IMDB.

00:02:07.293 --> 00:02:08.961
-I actually printed out
this IMDB.

00:02:08.961 --> 00:02:10.463
You're going to have to
really zoom in here.

00:02:10.463 --> 00:02:13.032
Look down where
it's highlighted here.

00:02:13.032 --> 00:02:15.001
-Yeah. It's really
right next to Tom. Yeah.

00:02:15.001 --> 00:02:16.769
-It's almost up next to Tom.

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:18.071
You keep calling him Tom, yeah.

00:02:18.071 --> 00:02:19.272
Beardo at the Bar.

00:02:19.272 --> 00:02:21.040
So they took Kevin
away from you?

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:23.476
-Yeah. And then I realized why.

00:02:23.476 --> 00:02:26.179
Because Beardo at the Bar is
such a great Marvel character,

00:02:26.179 --> 00:02:30.450
you know, and the idea of,
you know, we want to know more.

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:33.419
What's he doing at the bar?
How come a beard?

00:02:33.419 --> 00:02:35.287
That kind of stuff.
-Yeah. Those questions.

00:02:35.287 --> 00:02:37.857
-Yeah.
-Those questions spring up.

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:39.258
You go, "Yeah, yeah, yeah.
That's all good.

00:02:39.258 --> 00:02:41.394
-What's that guy's story?"
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.394 --> 00:02:44.396
-More about Beardo at the Bar.

00:02:44.396 --> 00:02:45.831
-I feel like you could --

00:02:45.831 --> 00:02:47.967
Don't you want him back
in the Marvel Universe, Beardo?

00:02:47.967 --> 00:02:49.969
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:52.438
I would love to see it.
-Thank you.

00:02:52.438 --> 00:02:55.241
-Nick, comedy clubs
are slowly opening up again.

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:58.711
Thank goodness.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:58.711 --> 00:03:03.349
It was tough on everybody,
and you're a great comedian.

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:04.984
Are you happy
to go back to clubs?

00:03:04.984 --> 00:03:07.119
-Yeah. Yeah.
In fact, I was at The Cellar

00:03:07.119 --> 00:03:10.389
all week here, going up
and got some new material.

00:03:10.389 --> 00:03:13.358
If you don't -- Me and the staff
all got together

00:03:13.358 --> 00:03:14.727
and got this for you.

00:03:14.727 --> 00:03:16.596
-Oh.

00:03:16.596 --> 00:03:17.897
The material?
-Yeah.

00:03:17.897 --> 00:03:20.032
-Oh, wow. Thank you.
Oh, this is fantastic.

00:03:20.032 --> 00:03:22.634
-Yeah.
So, this is a song I wrote.

00:03:22.634 --> 00:03:25.704
It's a song about a lost dog,
and it's hard to tell

00:03:25.704 --> 00:03:30.677
if I lost her or misplaced her
or what really happened.

00:03:30.677 --> 00:03:33.179
The song is called "Here, Girl,"
and this is something I wrote,

00:03:33.179 --> 00:03:35.381
you know, when I was really
creative over the...

00:03:35.381 --> 00:03:40.553
♪♪

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:43.856
[ Whistling ]

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:45.124
Here, girl, come on!

00:03:45.124 --> 00:03:47.560
[ Whistling ]

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:56.502
[ Laughter and applause ]
Thank you.

00:03:56.502 --> 00:03:57.570
-Beautiful.

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:58.972
-I've also been doing
some noodling.

00:03:58.972 --> 00:04:00.073
I don't know if you like noodles
or not.

00:04:00.073 --> 00:04:01.473
-Of course.

00:04:01.473 --> 00:04:03.075
-Well, I'd love to give you
a plate of them.

00:04:03.075 --> 00:04:09.214
♪♪

00:04:09.214 --> 00:04:13.286
You know, I was thinking
on my 35th birthday,

00:04:13.286 --> 00:04:14.419
I was in the kitchen
at my house.

00:04:14.419 --> 00:04:15.821
I was having a party.

00:04:15.821 --> 00:04:18.625
A friend came in and we were
just chatting, and he said,

00:04:18.625 --> 00:04:21.727
"Isn't it funny that the word
cupboard is spelled with a B

00:04:21.727 --> 00:04:23.362
but everyone thinks
that it's with a P?"

00:04:23.362 --> 00:04:25.531
[ Laughter ]

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:28.734
And I thought, "Yeah,
why would it be cup-board?

00:04:28.734 --> 00:04:30.736
That's dumb.
Of course it's with a B."

00:04:30.736 --> 00:04:33.439
So, anyway, three years go on.

00:04:33.439 --> 00:04:35.408
38th birthday,
I'm in the same kitchen.

00:04:35.408 --> 00:04:36.809
Same friend walks up to me
and he goes,

00:04:36.809 --> 00:04:38.911
"Oh, hey, by the way,
it is spelled with a P."

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:42.248
[ Laughter ]

00:04:42.248 --> 00:04:45.385
And that's three years
that I'll never get back.

00:04:45.385 --> 00:04:49.455
-Yeah, no, absolutely not.
-You know?

00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:52.458
Anyway, I know Memorial Day
is coming up and...

00:04:52.458 --> 00:04:56.028
[ Laughter ]

00:04:56.028 --> 00:04:57.296
You know, I support
the military,

00:04:57.296 --> 00:05:00.099
and I just think it's so sad

00:05:00.099 --> 00:05:02.034
that they only get one
4:20 a day.

00:05:02.034 --> 00:05:04.737
[ Laughter ]

00:05:04.737 --> 00:05:06.271
It's so early, you know,
and it's just --

00:05:06.271 --> 00:05:08.608
it's 16:20 when you're high.
It's so confusing.

00:05:08.608 --> 00:05:10.476
[ Laughter ]

00:05:10.476 --> 00:05:12.611
And, yes, Jimmy,
that is a military-time joke.

00:05:12.611 --> 00:05:14.313
[ Laughter ]
-Wow.

00:05:14.313 --> 00:05:16.149
-And if you don't mind,
I'd like to tell two more.

00:05:16.149 --> 00:05:17.916
[ Laughter ]
-We'd love it.

00:05:17.916 --> 00:05:19.352
-Or do I want to tell 14?

00:05:19.352 --> 00:05:22.822
[ Laughter ]

00:05:22.822 --> 00:05:25.624
I've got no idea.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:25.624 --> 00:05:26.992
You don't tell military time.

00:05:26.992 --> 00:05:28.493
Military tells you time.

00:05:28.493 --> 00:05:30.396
-Oh! That's what
I'm talking about.

00:05:30.396 --> 00:05:33.432
[ Applause ]
Nick Thune, everybody.

00:05:33.432 --> 00:05:36.235
That's noodling and some
deep thoughts right there.

00:05:36.235 --> 00:05:37.569
I love you, buddy.
Thanks so much.

00:05:37.569 --> 00:05:39.838
-Thanks for having me.
-Good to see you. Nick Thune!

00:05:39.838 --> 00:05:42.975
"The Right One" is available
on digital and on demand.

00:05:42.975 --> 00:05:44.911
Look for Beardo coming soon.

